-- title:
--   Iterated Frobenius rebase of a rigidification
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the Čerednik–Drinfeld frame for fake elliptic curves, and the hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, a positive integer $N$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. A discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ which is a domain of characteristic zero, with uniformiser $\pi$ (irreducible), $\pi$-adically complete, residue field of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$; a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A domain $Onr$ of characteristic zero, an $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo that ideal, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ having a root modulo that ideal, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^r$ modulo that ideal for all $x$: thus $Onr$ plays the role of the completion of the maximal unramified extension with its Frobenius. A homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) such that $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u \pi^n$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *Quaternionic data and moduli.* Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $a > 0$ or $b > 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is a division algebra at exactly the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ in it. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathcal O$ with a point map `pt` which by `h𝒳` makes $(\mathcal X, f)$ a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (isomorphism invariance, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a fine moduli scheme $(M,f_M)$ with point map `ptF` for curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), together with a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `IsLevelTwistAction` (the action is over the base, realises twisting of the level-$n$ structure by $\chi(g)$ on points, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base, invariant under $G$, compatible with the two point maps. Coarse moduli schemes $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with point maps for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure, indexed by the primes $\ell \neq r, \bar r$ (`h𝒴`), with two degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra structure and $d_1$ recording the $\ell$-isogeny quotient. Atkin–Lehner correspondences $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over the base, inducing on points the maps given by `IsAtkinLehnerQuotient` at $r$ and at $\bar r$.
--
--   *Definite quaternion side.* Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`, i.e. $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is a division algebra exactly at the place above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ inside it, an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the unit group, characterised as the group of units integral away from $v$ with respect to $R_1$; for each prime $\ell \neq r, \bar r$ elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ whose local components away from $r$ are $s_\ell$, whose component at $r$ is trivial, which lie in the appropriate level or prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ after multiplication by the diagonal $\ell$, and with $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; the congruence subgroups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   *Supersingular base point and its dictionary.* The hypothesis $h\Lambda_{\mathbb Z}$ that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$; a coordinate map `coord` on $\Lambda$ with values in $\mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, multiplicative in the twisted sense involving Frobenius, injective, dense, and compatible with traces). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over the residue ring $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over that ring, formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, with `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$ and $\theta_0$; endomorphisms $e(\gamma), e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with degrees $r^{\deg \gamma}$, over the base. The hypotheses `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act as scalars up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (converse: if $e\gamma$ becomes a scalar up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar), `hE2` (for any injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a conjugator $g$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0(\varepsilon) = r^{k_\gamma} g \iota_0(\gamma) g^{-1}$), `hE3` (the $e\gamma$ act on full level-$n$ structures through labels in $\Lambda$, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$), `hE4` (every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e\gamma$), the group `hE5a`–`hE5e` extending this dictionary from $\Gamma_t$ to an order $R_2 \le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation of $\hat e$, unitality, multiplicativity, scalars, the norm relation $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}(x)]$, compatibility with the $e\gamma$ up to $r$-powers, and a joint version of `hE2` for both $\Gamma_t$ and $R_2$), and `hJOINTw` (the joint version of `hE2` for $\Gamma_t$ together with a clause for the composite $a_w \circ b_w$ matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$).
--
--   *Drinfeld side.* A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to Onr$; a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $Onr/(r)$; a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf, with a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified formal modules to $MD$ satisfying `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidifications up to isomorphism, is compatible with base change, and is locally surjective on a Zariski cover); an injective ring map $E_0$ on the centraliser of the action on $\Phi$ with values in $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is, up to a fixed power of $r$, the set of integral matrices (`hE₀`). The comparison $e_D$ from the functor of points of $MD$ over $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with Drinfeld's functor of Deligne data $\Omega$, together with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the leg $\psi$), `hGLD` (the relation `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` for $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ corresponds under $e_D$ to the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`, which twists the leg by $Fr^{-vdet(g)}$ and pulls the Deligne datum back along $g^{-1}$), `hPiD` (the relation `IsPiTranslate` corresponds to twisting the leg by $Fr$ and leaving the datum fixed) and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates). Further: a ring map $\kappa$ from $Onr/(\pi)$ to $Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ exhibiting an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$.
--
--   *The supersingular dictionary $\Xi$.* A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; the Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on $A_0$, namely a curve $A_{0w}$, maps $a_w, a_w'$ realising `IsAtkinLehnerQuotientVia` at $\bar r$, and a level-preserving isogeny pair $b_w, b_w'$ of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ back to $A_0$. A map $\Xi$ assigning to each Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$, each leg $\psi : Onr \to B$ and each rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$ a $B$-point of $MD$ in the sense of `ModuliPackage.GPoint`, subject to: `hΞleg` (over $B$ with no nontrivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is $Fr^k$-twisted from $\psi$ for some $k \in \mathbb Z$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with base change along $\varphi$ of rigidifications), `hΞiso` (invariance of $\Xi$ under isomorphisms of rigidified curves compatible with the rigidification data up to $r$-powers) and `hΞdef` (for $B$ with connected spectrum and $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed by an admissible rigidified formal module $t$ obtained by transporting $\theta_0$, $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ through the rigidification, with a twist exponent $j \le 1$, and $\Xi$ equals the point $\langle Fr^{-j}\psi, \eta(t)\rangle$). Finally a matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and two equivariance clauses: `heqΓ`, stating that if two rigidifications of the same curve are related by translation by $e\gamma$ then $\Xi$ of the two is related by `IsActBy` for a central $r$-power times $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$; and `heqW`, the analogous statement for the Atkin–Lehner comparison at $\bar r$ (assuming $\bar r$ invertible on $B$), with $g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ in place of $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in $B$ and with no idempotents other than $0$ and $1$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, every rigidification $\rho$ of $E$ relative to the leg $\psi : Onr \to B$ and the base point $A_0$, every $k \in \mathbb Z$ and every $\psi' : Onr \to B$ with $\psi' = Fr^k \circ \psi$ (the hypothesis being the equation $\psi' =$ `frobTwist Onr Fr k ψ`), there exist a rigidification $\rho'$ of the same curve $E$ relative to $\psi'$ and an integer $c$ such that both of the following hold.
--
--   First, the relation `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` holds for the central element $(r \cdot 1)^c$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ between $\Xi_{B,\psi}(E,\rho)$ and $\Xi_{B,\psi'}(E,\rho')$: thus the two $MD$-points differ by the action of the scalar $r^c$.
--
--   Second, extra level structures away from $r$ transported through the two rigidifications have the same points: for every prime $\ell \neq r$ invertible in $B$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure $K_0$ on the base point $A_0$ and every pair of extra level-$\ell$ structures $C, C'$ on $E$, if $C$ is compatible with $K_0$ through $\rho$ — meaning that for every scheme $T$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(B/(\pi))$ and every $T$-point $R$ of the reduction $\rho.E_b$, whenever $R$ composed with $\rho.g_b$ factors through $C$ it follows that $R$ composed with $\rho.\varphi$ and then $\rho.g_A$ factors through $K_0$ — and if $C'$ is compatible with $K_0$ through $\rho'$ in the same sense, then $C$ and $C'$ cut out the same subfunctor of $E$: for every scheme $T$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,B$ and every $T$-point $R$ of $E$, $R$ factors through the closed immersion of $C$ if and only if it factors through that of $C'$.
--
--   This is the $\mathbb Z$-fold iterate of the one-step Frobenius rebase of a rigidification in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$: changing the unramified leg $\psi$ of a rigidified fake elliptic curve by an arbitrary power of Frobenius moves the associated Drinfeld datum only by a central scalar $r^c$, and leaves the prime-to-$r$ extra level structures unchanged. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld family over the fine moduli frame, where rigidifications with a prescribed parity of the Frobenius twist must be produced.
